From: Chimera core
Subject: [PATCH] New3D draws into the core's one buffer

With SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA, New3D gives the window back its front buffer,
not its back buffer, when it has finished with its own frame buffers.
The core draws with OSMesa, whose window has one buffer and no back
buffer: drawing to GL_BACK there draws nothing, and every frame read
back after it was black.
---
--- a/Src/Graphics/New3D/R3DFrameBuffers.cpp
+++ b/Src/Graphics/New3D/R3DFrameBuffers.cpp
@@ -180,7 +180,12 @@
 	case Layer::none:
 	{
 		glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+#ifdef SUPERMODEL_CHIMERA
+		// the Chimera core's window is OSMesa's one buffer (no back buffer)
+		glDrawBuffer(GL_FRONT);
+#else
 		glDrawBuffer(GL_BACK);
+#endif
 		break;
 	}
 	default:
